

kore-exec --help
KORE_EXEC_OPTS=''

kore-exec - an interpreter for Kore definitions

Usage: kore-exec [--version] 
                 [
                   [--search SEARCH_FILE [--bound BOUND]
                     --searchType SEARCH_TYPE] DEFINITION_FILE 
                   [--pattern PATTERN_FILE] [--output PATTERN_OUTPUT_FILE]
                   --module MODULE [--breadth BREADTH] [--depth DEPTH] 
                   [--strategy STRATEGY] [--smt-timeout SMT_TIMEOUT] 
                   [--smt-retry-limit SMT_RETRY_LIMIT] [--smt-rlimit SMT_RLIMIT]
                   [--smt-reset-interval SMT_RESET_INTERVAL] 
                   [--smt-prelude SMT_PRELUDE] [--smt SOLVER] 
                   [--smt-tactic SMT_TACTIC] [--smt-arg SMT_ARG] [--log ARG] 
                   [--log-format ARG] [--log-level ARG] 
                   [--enable-log-timestamps | --disable-log-timestamps] 
                   [--log-entries ARG] [--solver-transcript ARG] 
                   [--sqlog FILENAME] [--warnings-to-errors] 
                   [--error-entries ARG] 
                   [--debug-apply-equation EQUATION_IDENTIFIER] 
                   [--debug-attempt-equation EQUATION_IDENTIFIER] 
                   [--debug-equation EQUATION_IDENTIFIER] 
                   [--debug-attempt-rewrite REWRITE_RULE_IDENTIFIER] 
                   [--debug-apply-rewrite REWRITE_RULE_IDENTIFIER] 
                   [--debug-rewrite REWRITE_RULE_IDENTIFIER] 
                   [--trace-rewrites FILENAME] 
                   [--prove SPEC_FILE --spec-module SPEC_MODULE 
                     [--graph-search GRAPH_SEARCH] [--save-proofs ARG] 
                     [--disable-stuck-check] [--min-depth MIN_DEPTH] 
                     [--allow-vacuous] [--set-step-timeout INT] 
                     [--moving-average]] [--execute-to-branch] 
                   [--rts-statistics FILENAME] 
                   [--bug-report REPORT_FILE | --no-bug-report] 
                   [--max-counterexamples MAX_COUNTEREXAMPLES] 
                   [--[no-]serialize]]

  Uses Kore definition in DEFINITION_FILE to execute pattern in PATTERN_FILE.

Available options:
  --version                Print version information
  --search SEARCH_FILE     Kore source file representing pattern to search for.
                           Needs --module.
  --bound BOUND            Maximum number of solutions.
  --searchType SEARCH_TYPE Search type (selects potential solutions): ONE,
                           FINAL, STAR, PLUS
  DEFINITION_FILE          Kore definition file to verify and use for execution
  --pattern PATTERN_FILE   Verify and execute the Kore pattern found in
                           PATTERN_FILE.
  --output PATTERN_OUTPUT_FILE
                           Output file to contain final Kore pattern.
  --module MODULE          The name of the main module in the Kore definition.
  --breadth BREADTH        Allow up to BREADTH parallel execution branches.
  --depth DEPTH            Execute up to DEPTH steps.
  --strategy STRATEGY      Select rewrites using STRATEGY.
  --smt-timeout SMT_TIMEOUT
                           Timeout for calls to the SMT solver, in milliseconds
  --smt-retry-limit SMT_RETRY_LIMIT
                           Limit how many times an SMT query can be retried
                           (with scaling timeouts)
  --smt-rlimit SMT_RLIMIT  Resource limit for calls to the SMT solver
  --smt-reset-interval SMT_RESET_INTERVAL
                           Reset the solver after this number of queries
  --smt-prelude SMT_PRELUDE
                           Path to the SMT prelude file
  --smt SOLVER             SMT solver for checking constraints: z3, none
  --smt-tactic SMT_TACTIC  Z3 tactic to use when checking satisfiability.
                           Example: (check-sat-using smt)
  --smt-arg SMT_ARG        Argument passed to Z3
  --log ARG                Name of the log file
  --log-format ARG         Log format: standard, oneline, json
  --log-level ARG          Log level: debug, info, warning, error, or critical
  --enable-log-timestamps  Enable log timestamps
  --disable-log-timestamps Disable log timestamps
  --log-entries ARG        Log entries: comma-separated list logs entries to enable
                           Available entry types:
                               DebugSolverSend: log commands sent to SMT solver
                               DebugSolverRecv: log responses received from SMT solver
                               DebugTransition: log proof state
                               DebugAppliedRewriteRules: log applied rewrite rules
                               DebugAppliedLabeledRewriteRule: log applied rewrite rule with label
                               DebugRewriteRulesRemainder: log rewrite rules remainder
                               DebugAttemptedRewriteRules: log attempted rewrite rules
                               DebugSubstitutionSimplifier: log non-\bottom results when normalizing unification solutions
                               WarnFunctionWithoutEvaluators: warn when encountering a function with no definition
                               WarnSymbolSMTRepresentation: warn when a symbol cannot be translated for the SMT solver, despite being given an explicit translation
                               WarnStepTimeout: warn when a step has timed out
                               WarnStuckClaimState: distinguish the ways a proof can become stuck
                               WarnDepthLimitExceeded: warn when depth limit is exceeded
                               WarnClaimRHSIsBottom: warn when the right-hand side of a claim is bottom
                               WarnConfigIsBottom: warn when the configuration is bottom
                               WarnIfLowProductivity: warn when productivty (MUT time / Total time) drops below 90%
                               WarnTrivialClaim: warn when a claim is proven without taking any steps
                               WarnUnexploredBranches: indicate whether and how many unexplored branches existed when failing.
                               DebugRetrySolverQuery: warning raised when the solver failed to decide the satisfiability of a formula, indicating that the solver was reset and the formula retried
                               DebugUnifyBottom: log failed unification
                               DebugEvaluateCondition: log every predicate evaluated by the SMT solver
                               LogMessage: 
                               DebugAttemptUnification: log unification attempts
                               InfoReachability: log reachability proof steps
                               InfoExecBreadth: log number of concurrent branches
                               InfoUserLog: user-specified log message
                               DebugAttemptEquation: log equation application attempts
                               DebugApplyEquation: log equation application successes
                               DebugUnification: 
                               DebugTerm: 
                               InfoProofDepth: log depth of proof graph
                               InfoExecDepth: log depth of execution graph
                               DebugBeginClaim: log starting claims
                               DebugProven: log proven claims
                               WarnUnsimplifiedPredicate: warn when a predicate is not simplified
                               WarnUnsimplifiedCondition: warn when a condition is not simplified
                               WarnRestartSolver: warning raised to notify the user that the solver has crashed and the backend will attempt to restart it, reinitialise it and continue execution
                               DebugCreatedSubstitution: log every substitution created when applying semantic rules
                               DebugInitialClaim: log every claim before proving it
                               DebugInitialPattern: log initial pattern before rewriting
                               DebugFinalPatterns: log final patterns after rewriting
                               DebugRewriteTrace: log rewrite substitutions
                               LogJsonRpcServer: log JSON RPC Server messages
                               DebugContext: Debug message to signify an action's context
                               InfoJsonRpcProcessRequest: log valid requests to the JSON RPC server
                               InfoJsonRpcCancelRequest: log cancelled request to the JSON RPC server
                               ErrorBottomTotalFunction: errors raised when a total function is undefined
                               ErrorEquationRightFunction: errors raised when right-hand side of equation is not a function pattern
                               ErrorEquationsSameMatch: errors raised when two equations from a function definition can match the same term
                               ErrorOutOfDate: 
                               ErrorParse: 
                               ErrorVerify: 
                               ErrorException: log internal errors
                               ErrorRewriteLoop: 
                               ErrorRewritesInstantiation: log rewrite instantiation errors
                               DecidePredicateUnknown: error or a warning when the solver cannot decide the satisfiability of a formula
  --solver-transcript ARG  Name of the file for the SMT solver transcript.
  --sqlog FILENAME         Write the structured query log to FILENAME.
  --warnings-to-errors     Turn warnings into errors
  --error-entries ARG      Turn arbitrary log entries into errors
                           Available entry types:
                               DebugSolverSend: log commands sent to SMT solver
                               DebugSolverRecv: log responses received from SMT solver
                               DebugTransition: log proof state
                               DebugAppliedRewriteRules: log applied rewrite rules
                               DebugAppliedLabeledRewriteRule: log applied rewrite rule with label
                               DebugRewriteRulesRemainder: log rewrite rules remainder
                               DebugAttemptedRewriteRules: log attempted rewrite rules
                               DebugSubstitutionSimplifier: log non-\bottom results when normalizing unification solutions
                               WarnFunctionWithoutEvaluators: warn when encountering a function with no definition
                               WarnSymbolSMTRepresentation: warn when a symbol cannot be translated for the SMT solver, despite being given an explicit translation
                               WarnStepTimeout: warn when a step has timed out
                               WarnStuckClaimState: distinguish the ways a proof can become stuck
                               WarnDepthLimitExceeded: warn when depth limit is exceeded
                               WarnClaimRHSIsBottom: warn when the right-hand side of a claim is bottom
                               WarnConfigIsBottom: warn when the configuration is bottom
                               WarnIfLowProductivity: warn when productivty (MUT time / Total time) drops below 90%
                               WarnTrivialClaim: warn when a claim is proven without taking any steps
                               WarnUnexploredBranches: indicate whether and how many unexplored branches existed when failing.
                               DebugRetrySolverQuery: warning raised when the solver failed to decide the satisfiability of a formula, indicating that the solver was reset and the formula retried
                               DebugUnifyBottom: log failed unification
                               DebugEvaluateCondition: log every predicate evaluated by the SMT solver
                               LogMessage: 
                               DebugAttemptUnification: log unification attempts
                               InfoReachability: log reachability proof steps
                               InfoExecBreadth: log number of concurrent branches
                               InfoUserLog: user-specified log message
                               DebugAttemptEquation: log equation application attempts
                               DebugApplyEquation: log equation application successes
                               DebugUnification: 
                               DebugTerm: 
                               InfoProofDepth: log depth of proof graph
                               InfoExecDepth: log depth of execution graph
                               DebugBeginClaim: log starting claims
                               DebugProven: log proven claims
                               WarnUnsimplifiedPredicate: warn when a predicate is not simplified
                               WarnUnsimplifiedCondition: warn when a condition is not simplified
                               WarnRestartSolver: warning raised to notify the user that the solver has crashed and the backend will attempt to restart it, reinitialise it and continue execution
                               DebugCreatedSubstitution: log every substitution created when applying semantic rules
                               DebugInitialClaim: log every claim before proving it
                               DebugInitialPattern: log initial pattern before rewriting
                               DebugFinalPatterns: log final patterns after rewriting
                               DebugRewriteTrace: log rewrite substitutions
                               LogJsonRpcServer: log JSON RPC Server messages
                               DebugContext: Debug message to signify an action's context
                               InfoJsonRpcProcessRequest: log valid requests to the JSON RPC server
                               InfoJsonRpcCancelRequest: log cancelled request to the JSON RPC server
  --debug-apply-equation EQUATION_IDENTIFIER
                           Log every succesfully applied equation that matches
                           EQUATION_IDENTIFIER, which may be the name of a
                           symbol or a rule. The name of a symbol may be a Kore
                           identifier or a K label, which will match any
                           equation where the named symbol occurs on the
                           left-hand side. The name of a rule is given with the
                           K module name as a dot-separated prefix:
                           'MODULE-NAME.rule-name'. This option may be specified
                           multiple times to log multiple equations.
  --debug-attempt-equation EQUATION_IDENTIFIER
                           Log every attempt to apply an equation that matches
                           EQUATION_IDENTIFIER, which may be the name of a
                           symbol or a rule. It will not be mentioned whether
                           the application succeeds or not. The name of a symbol
                           may be a Kore identifier or a K label, which will
                           match any equation where the named symbol occurs on
                           the left-hand side. The name of a rule is given with
                           the K module name as a dot-separated prefix:
                           'MODULE-NAME.rule-name'. This option may be specified
                           multiple times to log multiple equations.
  --debug-equation EQUATION_IDENTIFIER
                           Log every attempt to apply or successful application
                           of an equation that matches EQUATION_IDENTIFIER,
                           which may be the name of a symbol or a rule. The name
                           of a symbol may be a Kore identifier or a K label,
                           which will match any equation where the named symbol
                           occurs on the left-hand side. The name of a rule is
                           given with the K module name as a dot-separated
                           prefix: 'MODULE-NAME.rule-name'. This option may be
                           specified multiple times to log multiple equations.
  --debug-attempt-rewrite REWRITE_RULE_IDENTIFIER
                           Log every attempt to apply an rewrite rule that
                           matches REWRITE_RULE_IDENTIFIER, which may be the
                           name of a symbol or a rule. It will not be mentioned
                           whether the application succeeds or not. The name of
                           a symbol may be a Kore identifier or a K label, which
                           will match any equation where the named symbol occurs
                           on the left-hand side. The name of a rule is given
                           with the K module name as a dot-separated prefix:
                           'MODULE-NAME.rule-name'. This option may be specified
                           multiple times to log multiple equations.
  --debug-apply-rewrite REWRITE_RULE_IDENTIFIER
                           Log every succesfully applied rewrite rule that
                           matches REWRITE_RULE_IDENTIFIER, which may be the
                           name of a symbol or a rule. The name of a symbol may
                           be a Kore identifier or a K label, which will match
                           any equation where the named symbol occurs on the
                           left-hand side. The name of a rule is given with the
                           K module name as a dot-separated prefix:
                           'MODULE-NAME.rule-name'. This option may be specified
                           multiple times to log multiple equations.
  --debug-rewrite REWRITE_RULE_IDENTIFIER
                           Log every attempt to apply or successful application
                           of an rewrite rule that matches
                           REWRITE_RULE_IDENTIFIER, which may be the name of a
                           symbol or a rule. The name of a symbol may be a Kore
                           identifier or a K label, which will match any
                           equation where the named symbol occurs on the
                           left-hand side. The name of a rule is given with the
                           K module name as a dot-separated prefix:
                           'MODULE-NAME.rule-name'. This option may be specified
                           multiple times to log multiple equations.
  --trace-rewrites FILENAME
                           Output rewrite trace to a YAML file
  --prove SPEC_FILE        Kore source file representing spec to be proven.Needs
                           --spec-module.
  --spec-module SPEC_MODULE
                           The name of the main module in the spec to be proven.
  --graph-search GRAPH_SEARCH
                           Search order of the execution graph. Either
                           breadth-first or depth-first. Default is
                           breadth-first.
  --save-proofs ARG        The file in which to save the proven claims in case
                           the prover fails.
  --disable-stuck-check    Disable the heuristic for detecting stuck states.
  --min-depth MIN_DEPTH    Force the prover to execute at least n steps.
  --allow-vacuous          Enables discharging #Bottom paths as #Top at
                           implication checking time.
  --set-step-timeout INT   Set a timeout for one step in seconds.
  --moving-average         Enable timeout based on moving average.
  --execute-to-branch      Execute until the proof branches.
  --rts-statistics FILENAME
                           Write runtime statistics to FILENAME in JSON format.
  --bug-report REPORT_FILE Generate reproducible example of bug at
                           REPORT_FILE.tar.gz
  --no-bug-report          Disables the creation of a bug report.
  --max-counterexamples MAX_COUNTEREXAMPLES
                           Specify the maximum number of counterexamples.
  --[no-]serialize         Enable/disable serialization of initialized
                           definition to disk. [default: disabled]
  -h,--help                Show this help text
